CuteMouse 2.1 beta 4 (FreeDOS CTMOUSE), GPL v2 (src/copying).
Source: https://github.com/FDOS/mouse, commit dd268521dc76d323d0597d1b21f58be5b82c6c25.

CTMOUSE.COM is prebuilt so the normal build needs no extra tools. It talks to
the mouse through the BIOS PS/2 services (INT 15h C2xx, src/bios.c), which
vmdos provides on top of its virtual PS/2 mouse port.

Changes, for JWasm 2.21 (case-sensitive includes, stricter structures):
lower-case include paths; "STRUCT ?" written as "STRUCT <?,...>" (still
uninitialised, so the overlap with the PSP is kept); area0.def "STRUCT ?"
as "<>" (AT segment, no data emitted); "say S_mousetype[si]" written out as
mov di,S_mousetype[si] / call sayASCIIZ.

Rebuild: tools/build-ctmouse.sh (needs JWasm and Open Watcom's wlink and
exe2bin on PATH).
